            <ArticleTitle>[Pregnancy termination between 12 and 14 weeks gestation: practices and early complications in comparison with termination between 8 and 12 weeks].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>339-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVES" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To describe and compare practices and complications of induced abortions (IA) between 12 and 14 gestational weeks (GW) with those performed at lower terms (8-10 and 10-12 GW).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PATIENTS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Cohort study enrolled in two IA centers 411 women, 147 of them with 12-14 weeks gestation. Comparisons were made according to pregnancy term (8-10, 10-12 and 12-14 GW).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Pregnancy term influenced the technical conditions of IA. Number and diameter of dilators and suction cannula as well as surgery time increase with gestational age--whether priming agents were used or not. Pain felt during surgery and early complications (within 15 days post IA) did not increase with gestational age.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Results of this study show that IA between 12 and 14 GW are as feasible as with lower terms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
